    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_32">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-citation-items=&quot;%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22itemData%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22article-journal%22%2C%22abstract%22%3A%22Background%3A%20Beneficial%20mutations%20play%20an%20essential%20role%20in%20bacterial%20adaptation%2C%20yet%20little%20is%20known%20about%20their%20fitness%20effects%20across%20genetic%20backgrounds%20and%20environments.%20One%20prominent%20example%20of%20bacterial%20adaptation%20is%20antibiotic%20resistance.%20Until%20recently%2C%20the%20paradigm%20has%20been%20that%20antibiotic%20resistance%20is%20selected%20by%20the%20presence%20of%20antibiotics%20because%20resistant%20mutations%20confer%20fitness%20costs%20in%20antibiotic%20free%20environments.%20In%20this%20study%20we%20show%20that%20it%20is%20not%20always%20the%20case%2C%20documenting%20the%20selection%20and%20fixation%20of%20resistant%20mutations%20in%20populations%20of%20Escherichia%20coli%20B%20that%20had%20never%20been%20exposed%20to%20antibiotics%20but%20instead%20evolved%20for%202000%20generations%20at%20high%20temperature%20(42.2%C2%B0C).%5CnResults%3A%20We%20found%20parallel%20mutations%20within%20the%20rpoB%20gene%20encoding%20the%20beta%20subunit%20of%20RNA%20polymerase.%20These%20amino%20acid%20substitutions%20conferred%20different%20levels%20of%20rifampicin%20resistance.%20The%20resistant%20mutations%20typically%20appeared%2C%20and%20were%20fixed%2C%20early%20in%20the%20evolution%20experiment.%20We%20confirmed%20the%20high%20advantage%20of%20these%20mutations%20at%2042.2%C2%B0C%20in%20glucose-limited%20medium.%20However%2C%20the%20rpoB%20mutations%20had%20different%20fitness%20effects%20across%20three%20genetic%20backgrounds%20and%20six%20environments.%5CnConclusions%3A%20We%20describe%20resistance%20mutations%20that%20are%20not%20necessarily%20costly%20in%20the%20absence%20of%20antibiotics%20or%20compensatory%20mutations%20but%20are%20highly%20beneficial%20at%20high%20temperature%20and%20low%20glucose.%20Their%20fitness%20effects%20depend%20on%20the%20environment%20and%20the%20genetic%20background%2C%20providing%20glimpses%20into%20the%20prevalence%20of%20epistasis%20and%20pleiotropy.%22%2C%22container-title%22%3A%22BMC%20Evolutionary%20Biology%22%2C%22DOI%22%3A%2210.1186%2F1471-2148-13-50%22%2C%22ISSN%22%3A%221471-2148%22%2C%22issue%22%3A%221%22%2C%22journalAbbreviation%22%3A%22BMC%20Evol%20Biol%22%2C%22language%22%3A%22en%22%2C%22page%22%3A%2250%22%2C%22source%22%3A%22DOI.org%20(Crossref)%22%2C%22title%22%3A%22Evolution%20of%20Escherichia%20coli%20rifampicin%20resistance%20in%20an%20antibiotic-free%20environment%20during%20thermal%20stress%22%2C%22URL%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fbmcevolbiol.biomedcentral.com%2Farticles%2F10.1186%2F1471-2148-13-50%22%2C%22volume%22%3A%2213%22%2C%22author%22%3A%5B%7B%22family%22%3A%22Rodr%C3%ADguez-Verdugo%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Alejandra%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Gaut%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Brandon%20S%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Tenaillon%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Olivier%22%7D%5D%2C%22accessed%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222026%22%2C1%2C20%5D%5D%7D%2C%22issued%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222013%22%2C12%5D%5D%7D%7D%7D%5D&quot; data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FXW5JCUVY%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%229%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A8%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B56.69349136981393%2C274.5647883288631%2C290.529886259811%2C283.5414967746631%5D%2C%5B56.69349136981393%2C262.4775915091941%2C290.516172567014%2C272.27749155919406%5D%2C%5B56.69250883183494%2C250.58443280851407%2C290.46128494156324%2C259.56114125431407%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%229%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“the long fixation time in these lines could be due in part to negative epistatic interactions between rho and rpoB mutations that reduces beneficial effects of both mutations.”&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FXW5JCUVY%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%229%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A8%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B324.96369286600134%2C442.5485933791781%2C538.5534943753929%2C451.5253018249781%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C430.5868353781481%2C538.5485946881035%2C439.5635438239481%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C418.5682378588291%2C463.00998503086913%2C427.5449463046291%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%229%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“a single beneficial mutation is unlikely to result in niche specialization, because it will not lead to drastic fitness differences across environment”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%229%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Rodríguez-Verdugo et al., 2013, p. 9&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FXW5JCUVY%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%229%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A8%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B312.718717689925%2C406.5496403395101%2C538.5505542832709%2C415.5263487853101%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C394.58788233848014%2C538.5476141410721%2C403.56459078428014%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C382.5692848191611%2C538.5505543560845%2C391.5459932649611%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C370.48208799949214%2C538.5515338485487%2C380.2819880494921%5D%2C%5B304.725919209145%2C358.58892929881216%2C538.5417342688571%2C367.56563774461216%5D%2C%5B304.725919209145%2C346.57033177949313%2C495.81319029957785%2C355.54704022529313%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%229%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“In stark contrast to these studies, we do observe the potential for the evolution of ecological specialization in a single mutational step, because all three mutations in codon 572 of rpoB confer a selective advantage in the conditions of the original evolution experiment but significant disadvantages in other environments”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%229%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Rodríguez-Verdugo et al., 2013, p. 9&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FXW5JCUVY%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%229%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A8%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B452.4979768048373%2C634.5636498085311%2C538.4989597371257%2C643.5403582543311%5D%2C%5B304.7243042%2C622.5450522892121%2C538.4930800922685%2C631.5217607350121%5D%2C%5B304.7243042%2C610.5832942881821%2C538.4921001075555%2C619.5600027339821%5D%2C%5B304.7243042%2C598.5646967688631%2C538.5518794922747%2C607.5414052146631%5D%2C%5B304.7243042%2C586.54440553785%2C538.627973749639%2C597.68750401749%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C574.58264753682%2C538.6985326701468%2C583.55935598262%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C562.564050017501%2C538.5593747515182%2C571.540758463301%5D%2C%5B304.72493921913997%2C550.545452498182%2C440.5505735712983%2C559.522160943982%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%229%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“in our study, the only environment in which the mutations are demonstrably beneficial is that of the original evolution experiment (high temperature and low glucose). In contrast, the effects of rifR mutations are indistinguishable from neutrality in a high temperature and rich glucose environment and demonstrably detrimental at 37°C in poor and rich glucose environment”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FNUNPGIHK%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%229%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Rodríguez-Verdugo et al., 2013, p. 9&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Big picture and motivation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The paper challenges a classic assumption in evolutionary microbiology:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Antibiotic resistance mutations are usually costly and only selected in the presence of antibiotics.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Instead, the authors show that &lt;strong&gt;rifampicin resistance mutations can evolve, spread, and even be strongly beneficial in an antibiotic-free environment&lt;/strong&gt;, purely as a by-product of adaptation to &lt;strong&gt;thermal stress and nutrient limitation&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They use &lt;strong&gt;long-term experimental evolution of &lt;em&gt;E. coli&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to demonstrate how &lt;strong&gt;environment, genetic background, pleiotropy, and epistasis&lt;/strong&gt; shape the fate of resistance mutations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Experimental system&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Organism:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/em&gt; B
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Starting strain:&lt;/strong&gt; REL1206
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolution conditions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
42.2 °C (high thermal stress)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Davis minimal medium with &lt;strong&gt;low glucose (DM25)&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
No antibiotics
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
114 independent populations
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
2,000 generations
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Whole-genome sequences available for endpoint clones
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Central questions&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Do antibiotic resistance mutations arise without antibiotics?&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;If yes, what mutations are involved and when do they appear?&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Are these mutations actually beneficial under the evolution conditions?&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;How do their fitness effects depend on environment and genetic background?&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key findings&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;1. Rifampicin resistance evolved without antibiotics&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;13 out of 114 evolved clones&lt;/strong&gt; were resistant to rifampicin
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Resistance was defined by &lt;strong&gt;elevated MIC values (≥ 25 µg/mL)&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
This occurred &lt;strong&gt;despite zero exposure to antibiotics&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 This alone contradicts the idea that resistance must be directly selected by drugs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;2. Resistance is caused by parallel mutations in &lt;em&gt;rpoB&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Rifampicin resistance mapped almost entirely to &lt;strong&gt;single amino-acid substitutions in &lt;em&gt;rpoB&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (RNA polymerase β-subunit)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12 of 13 resistant clones&lt;/strong&gt; carried mutations at &lt;strong&gt;codon 572&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;I572N&lt;/strong&gt; → intermediate resistance
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;I572L&lt;/strong&gt; → high resistance
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;I572F&lt;/strong&gt; → very high resistance (&amp;gt; 800 µg/mL)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
These mutations arose &lt;strong&gt;independently in multiple populations&lt;/strong&gt;, a strong signal of &lt;strong&gt;positive selection&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;3. Resistance mutations appeared early and often fixed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Resistance typically appeared within &lt;strong&gt;the first 500 generations&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
In &lt;strong&gt;10 of 12 populations&lt;/strong&gt;, resistance went to fixation (&amp;gt; 90%)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Earlier-appearing mutations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Increased in frequency faster
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Fixed more rapidly
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Importantly:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Fixation speed was not determined solely by mutation strength&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Timing, clonal interference, and epistasis mattered more than raw fitness advantage
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;4. &lt;em&gt;rpoB&lt;/em&gt; mutations are strongly beneficial at high temperature&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The authors reconstructed each mutation individually in the ancestral background.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Under &lt;strong&gt;42.2 °C + low glucose (DM25)&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
All three &lt;em&gt;rpoB&lt;/em&gt; mutations increased fitness by &lt;strong&gt;~18–25%&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
These are &lt;strong&gt;exceptionally large fitness effects&lt;/strong&gt; for single mutations
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Fitness benefits were &lt;strong&gt;significant even without antibiotics&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;➡️ These mutations were selected &lt;strong&gt;because they improved growth under thermal stress&lt;/strong&gt;, not because they conferred resistance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;5. Fitness effects depend strongly on genetic background (epistasis)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same &lt;em&gt;rpoB&lt;/em&gt; mutations were introduced into:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;em&gt;E. coli&lt;/em&gt; B REL606
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;em&gt;E. coli&lt;/em&gt; K-12 MG1655
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Results:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;REL606:&lt;/strong&gt; mutations beneficial (similar to REL1206)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MG1655:&lt;/strong&gt; mutations deleterious or lethal&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
One mutation (I572N) could not even be constructed
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👉 This is clear &lt;strong&gt;genotype-by-genotype interaction (epistasis)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;A mutation that is strongly beneficial in one strain can be harmful in another&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;6. Fitness effects also depend on environment (G×E interactions)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fitness was tested across &lt;strong&gt;five environments&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Different temperatures (37 °C vs 42.2 °C)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Different glucose levels
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Rich vs minimal media
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Findings:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mutations were:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Beneficial only at high temperature + low glucose&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Neutral or deleterious&lt;/strong&gt; in all other environments
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
At 37 °C (standard lab conditions), mutations were &lt;strong&gt;consistently costly&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This shows strong &lt;strong&gt;environment-specific adaptation and pleiotropy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Interpretation and broader significance&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why is this important?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Antibiotic resistance can evolve without antibiotics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Resistance may arise as a side-effect of adaptation to other stresses
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resistance mutations are not inherently costly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Their effects depend on &lt;strong&gt;context&lt;/strong&gt;, not just function
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Single mutations can drive ecological specialization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
These &lt;em&gt;rpoB&lt;/em&gt; mutations are beneficial in one niche and harmful in others
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transcription machinery is a major adaptive target&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Changes in RNA polymerase can globally reshape gene expression
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Likely mechanism for coping with thermal stress
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Core takeaway&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rifampicin resistance in &lt;em&gt;E. coli&lt;/em&gt; can be a by-product of thermal adaptation, driven by highly beneficial &lt;em&gt;rpoB&lt;/em&gt; mutations whose effects depend strongly on genetic background and environment.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This paper reframes antibiotic resistance as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
an evolutionary phenomenon shaped by &lt;strong&gt;pleiotropy, epistasis, and environmental specificity&lt;/strong&gt;,
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
not just a response to drug exposure.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
