        <dc:title>Deciphering the Impact of Temperature on Pleiotropic Consequences of RNA Polymerase Mutations</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Despite occurring in an essential molecule, mutations in RNA polymerase readily emerge and elicit complex pleiotropic effects across different levels of biological organization, which are all modulated by environment. We investigated the impact of temperature on the effects of six mutations on sequence, structure, transcriptome, and organismal traits. We found temperature altered the transcriptomic response and key organismal traits such as growth rate and biofilm formation in a genotype-specific manner. Critically, mechanistic insights into the possible drivers of mutational effects emerged only when examining the relationships between different levels of organization: location of mutations in the tertiary structure and distance to key interacting molecules partly explained the observed transcriptomic differences, which in turn drove the impact of mutations on organismal traits. While falling short of capturing the full complexity of the system, our findings underscore the benefits of integrating insights across multiple biological levels to understand the relationship between environment and mutational effects in molecules with extensive pleiotropic effects.</dcterms:abstract>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:libraryCatalog>Zotero</z:libraryCatalog>
    </bib:Article>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_65">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-citation-items=&quot;%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22itemData%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22article-journal%22%2C%22abstract%22%3A%22Despite%20occurring%20in%20an%20essential%20molecule%2C%20mutations%20in%20RNA%20polymerase%20readily%20emerge%20and%20elicit%20complex%20pleiotropic%20effects%20across%20different%20levels%20of%20biological%20organization%2C%20which%20are%20all%20modulated%20by%20environment.%20We%20investigated%20the%20impact%20of%20temperature%20on%20the%20effects%20of%20six%20mutations%20on%20sequence%2C%20structure%2C%20transcriptome%2C%20and%20organismal%20traits.%20We%20found%20temperature%20altered%20the%20transcriptomic%20response%20and%20key%20organismal%20traits%20such%20as%20growth%20rate%20and%20biofilm%20formation%20in%20a%20genotype-specific%20manner.%20Critically%2C%20mechanistic%20insights%20into%20the%20possible%20drivers%20of%20mutational%20effects%20emerged%20only%20when%20examining%20the%20relationships%20between%20different%20levels%20of%20organization%3A%20location%20of%20mutations%20in%20the%20tertiary%20structure%20and%20distance%20to%20key%20interacting%20molecules%20partly%20explained%20the%20observed%20transcriptomic%20differences%2C%20which%20in%20turn%20drove%20the%20impact%20of%20mutations%20on%20organismal%20traits.%20While%20falling%20short%20of%20capturing%20the%20full%20complexity%20of%20the%20system%2C%20our%20findings%20underscore%20the%20benefits%20of%20integrating%20insights%20across%20multiple%20biological%20levels%20to%20understand%20the%20relationship%20between%20environment%20and%20mutational%20effects%20in%20molecules%20with%20extensive%20pleiotropic%20effects.%22%2C%22language%22%3A%22en%22%2C%22source%22%3A%22Zotero%22%2C%22title%22%3A%22Deciphering%20the%20Impact%20of%20Temperature%20on%20Pleiotropic%20Consequences%20of%20RNA%20Polymerase%20Mutations%22%2C%22author%22%3A%5B%7B%22family%22%3A%22Ozbilek%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Deniz%22%7D%5D%7D%7D%5D&quot; data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FHARWKQRA%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%223%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A2%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B477.70050000000026%2C47.36825%2C560.9838000000002%2C56.00775%5D%2C%5B317.7125%2C36.370000000000005%2C560.9727000000003%2C45.0095%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%223%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“the distance between the mutated residues and the nontemplate strand of DNA,”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%223%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Ozbilek, p. 3&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FHARWKQRA%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%224%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A3%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B280.96927500000004%2C706.6958476%2C294.326275%2C716.1385%5D%2C%5B51.024450000000016%2C696.50075%2C294.3198%2C705.14025%5D%2C%5B51.024450000000016%2C685.5025%2C294.29297500000007%2C694.142%5D%2C%5B51.024450000000016%2C674.5042500000001%2C294.265225%2C683.1437500000001%5D%2C%5B51.024450000000016%2C663.506%2C294.29760000000005%2C672.1455%5D%2C%5B51.024450000000016%2C652.50775%2C243.32270000000005%2C661.14725%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%224%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“We hypothesize that mutations closer to these key sites have the potential to exert a stronger effect on RNAP function and therefore have a greater influence on fitness—a hypothesis we will test in relation to transcriptomic- and organismal-level effects of rpoB mutations in subsequent sections”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%224%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Ozbilek, p. 4&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FHARWKQRA%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%224%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A3%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B377.85805000000005%2C564.461475%2C555.592175%2C573.100975%5D%2C%5B312.320875%2C553.463225%2C555.573675%2C562.102725%5D%2C%5B312.320875%2C542.46405%2C555.592175%2C551.10355%5D%2C%5B312.320875%2C531.4658%2C476.7886500000001%2C540.1052999999999%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%224%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“Instead, our data shows that the response to temperature change is dominated by the effects of rpoB mutations, which substantially alter the transcriptomic response to temperature in genotype-specific manner.”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%224%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Ozbilek, p. 4&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FHARWKQRA%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%225%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A4%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B378.7090500000001%2C344.38495%2C560.9886249999998%2C353.02445%5D%2C%5B317.70345000000003%2C333.3867%2C560.9340500000003%2C342.0262%5D%2C%5B317.70345000000003%2C322.38845000000003%2C337.4300000000001%2C331.02795000000003%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%225%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“While many factors might impact bacterial growth, overexpression of metabolic genes is certainly one of them”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%225%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Ozbilek, p. 5&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FHARWKQRA%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%225%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A4%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B400.02472500000033%2C300.3873%2C560.993225%2C309.0268%5D%2C%5B317.7062%2C289.38905%2C560.9913750000001%2C298.02855%5D%2C%5B317.7062%2C278.3908%2C560.988575%2C287.03125%5D%2C%5B317.7034%2C267.3926%2C406.5154250000003%2C276.033%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%225%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“both Q513R and S531F were found to overexpress genes involved in the production of ATP-synthase (atpA/C/G/D)—a ubiquitously expressed enzyme shown to maximize growth rate”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%225%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Ozbilek, p. 5&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FHARWKQRA%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%225%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A4%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B545.7241999999999%2C267.3926%2C560.9348999999997%2C276.033%5D%2C%5B317.70799999999997%2C256.39435000000003%2C560.9950249999999%2C265.03385000000003%5D%2C%5B317.70799999999997%2C245.39610000000002%2C560.9534249999997%2C254.03650000000002%5D%2C%5B317.7034%2C234.39875%2C560.9589749999996%2C243.03825%5D%2C%5B317.7034%2C223.4005%2C560.9830249999998%2C232.04%5D%2C%5B317.7034%2C212.40040000000002%2C560.99875%2C221.04174999999998%5D%2C%5B317.7062%2C201.4022%2C348.8824000000001%2C210.0417%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%225%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“The same two mutants also overexpressed genes that are a part of the pyruvate dehydrogenase complex (aceE/F) as well as genes involved in phosphorylation of pyruvate (ppsA) and conversion of L-lactate to pyruvate (lldD). Pyruvate is essential for aerobic growth and has been shown to increase the rate of aerobic respiration”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F58AVRU9Z%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%225%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Ozbilek, p. 5&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
