    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_233">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-citation-items=&quot;%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FGRQ6I4BP%22%5D%2C%22itemData%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FGRQ6I4BP%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22article-journal%22%2C%22abstract%22%3A%22Specific%20small%20deletions%20within%20the%5Cn%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20rpoC%5Cn%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20gene%20encoding%20the%20%CE%B2%E2%80%B2-subunit%20of%20RNA%20polymerase%20(RNAP)%20are%20found%20repeatedly%20after%20adaptation%20of%5Cn%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20Escherichia%20coli%5Cn%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20K-12%20MG1655%20to%20growth%20in%20minimal%20media.%20Here%20we%20present%20a%20multiscale%20analysis%20of%20these%20mutations.%20At%20the%20physiological%20level%2C%20the%20mutants%20grow%2060%25%20faster%20than%20the%20parent%20strain%20and%20convert%20the%20carbon%20source%2015%E2%80%9335%25%20more%20efficiently%20to%20biomass%2C%20but%20grow%20about%2030%25%20slower%20than%20the%20parent%20strain%20in%20rich%20medium.%20At%20the%20molecular%20level%2C%20the%20kinetic%20parameters%20of%20the%20mutated%20RNAP%20were%20found%20to%20be%20altered%2C%20resulting%20in%20a%204-%20to%2030-fold%20decrease%20in%20open%20complex%20longevity%20at%20an%20rRNA%20promoter%20and%20a%20%E2%88%BC10-fold%20decrease%20in%20transcriptional%20pausing%2C%20with%20consequent%20increase%20in%20transcript%20elongation%20rate.%20At%20a%20genome-scale%2C%20systems%20biology%20level%2C%20gene%20expression%20changes%20between%20the%20parent%20strain%20and%20adapted%20RNAP%20mutants%20reveal%20large-scale%20systematic%20transcriptional%20changes%20that%20influence%20specific%20cellular%20processes%2C%20including%20strong%20down-regulation%20of%20motility%2C%20acid%20resistance%2C%20fimbria%2C%20and%20curlin%20genes.%20RNAP%20genome-binding%20maps%20reveal%20redistribution%20of%20RNAP%20that%20may%20facilitate%20relief%20of%20a%20metabolic%20bottleneck%20to%20growth.%20These%20findings%20suggest%20that%20reprogramming%20the%20kinetic%20parameters%20of%20RNAP%20through%20specific%20mutations%20allows%20regulatory%20adaptation%20for%20optimal%20growth%20in%20new%20environments.%22%2C%22container-title%22%3A%22Proceedings%20of%20the%20National%20Academy%20of%20Sciences%22%2C%22DOI%22%3A%2210.1073%2Fpnas.0911253107%22%2C%22ISSN%22%3A%220027-8424%2C%201091-6490%22%2C%22issue%22%3A%2247%22%2C%22journalAbbreviation%22%3A%22Proc.%20Natl.%20Acad.%20Sci.%20U.S.A.%22%2C%22language%22%3A%22en%22%2C%22page%22%3A%2220500-20505%22%2C%22source%22%3A%22DOI.org%20(Crossref)%22%2C%22title%22%3A%22RNA%20polymerase%20mutants%20found%20through%20adaptive%20evolution%20reprogram%20%3Ci%3EEscherichia%20coli%3C%2Fi%3E%20for%20optimal%20growth%20in%20minimal%20media%22%2C%22URL%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fpnas.org%2Fdoi%2Ffull%2F10.1073%2Fpnas.0911253107%22%2C%22volume%22%3A%22107%22%2C%22author%22%3A%5B%7B%22family%22%3A%22Conrad%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Tom%20M.%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Frazier%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Michael%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Joyce%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Andrew%20R.%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Cho%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Byung-Kwan%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Knight%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Eric%20M.%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Lewis%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Nathan%20E.%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Landick%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Robert%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Palsson%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Bernhard%20%C3%98.%22%7D%5D%2C%22accessed%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222026%22%2C1%2C23%5D%5D%7D%2C%22issued%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222010%22%2C11%2C23%5D%5D%7D%7D%7D%5D&quot; data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F3WJZEBXL%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%221%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A0%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B218.04519928999989%2C194.5034095%2C287.88550324999994%2C202.8151696%5D%2C%5B42.85894%2C184.333835%2C188.80608814999997%2C192.7800896%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FGRQ6I4BP%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%221%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“ppGpp is required for growth of E. coli in minimal media”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FGRQ6I4BP%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%221%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Conrad et al., 2010, p. 1&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Fig. 1, the &lt;strong&gt;rifampicin-resistant strains&lt;/strong&gt; (rpoB8, rpoB2, rpoB114) are included mainly for &lt;strong&gt;comparison&lt;/strong&gt;, not as the primary experimental focus. For some strain–medium combinations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
the strains &lt;strong&gt;did not grow reliably&lt;/strong&gt;, or
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
the experiments were &lt;strong&gt;not performed&lt;/strong&gt;, or
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
growth was &lt;strong&gt;too poor/inconsistent&lt;/strong&gt; to calculate a valid growth rate
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So instead of plotting misleading values, they label those conditions as &lt;strong&gt;n.d&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
